      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}\n\nI missed your reply until just now, but it's all entirely fair. I don't expect every single thing made to be mindful of colorblind people, but always like to push for awareness when I notice something isn't (or if it loses the band-aid that allows it to be like in this case)😁\n\nTo be fully honest, I think my \"real\" opinion is that the trust rating system is probably not relevant often enough to be broadcast on someone's nameplate, and more often gets used in a way to assist people to discriminate based on hours played. So an alternative \"fix\" in the end could just as easily be removing the shield entirely from the nameplate and just having trust ratings only be visible on the user profile screen (where it still has the text, and thus makes everyone equal opportunity in the steps to see it). Kinda two birds, one stone in that regard. Makes the trust rating less noteworthy by hiding it away while also having the primary resource to check that be colorblind friendly since it's written out.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
